>with our rewrites to DECforms. 

The syntax is so fragile that when the parser finds a syntax error,
it finds nothing but syntax errors after that, so you have to fix the 
first one and recompile to find the second one.

>Could you tell me who has the Visual Basic support?  That's one of the 
>programs I've been looking into using. I also have an evaluation copy of 
>Micro Focus Visual Object COBOL that I've been looking at.
>
>Could you also tell me where I can go to get info on a Windows client 
>generator?

I was really impressed with DECADMIRE, which generates VMS code in many 
languages, IFDL, and ACMS for you.  I never used it because we are a small
development operation and its price was out of our reach, but if 32,000 
lines is 10% of your project, its price will be a bargain.  The current
release will generate IFDL for VMS or ACMS terminals, and it will also
generate Visual Basic for PCs.  Get a trial copy.

Good luck,
