In article <1996Jul26.015856.1@eds.ericsson.se>, etxjesm@eds.ericsson.se writes:
<snip>
:      Standalone  Backup  is no longer part of the OpenVMS AXP operating
:      system.  Please refer to the "Backing Up and Restoring the  System
:      Disk"  appendix  in  the  "OpenVMS  AXP  Upgrade  and Installation
:      Manual" for more information.
:
:      After  reading  the information in the manual, you may wish to use
:      the procedure  SYS$SYSTEM:AXPVMS$PCSI_INSTALL_MIN.COM  to  install
:      OpenVMS  AXP  without any optional features on one or more of your
:      "data disks".  
<snip>
:  Does this mean that this system actualy is bootable from
:  another disk and not only the CD ?

  OpenVMS Alpha has always been bootable only from disk. 

  With OpenVMS Alpha V6.1 and later, one can boot a "single user" OpenVMS
  environment from CD-ROM (Digital offers extra copies of the necessary
  CD-ROM for about US$12, a copy of the CD-ROM ships with the OpenVMS
  distribution kit), and one can boot from a locally created magnetic
  disk.  

  The STABACKIT capability of creating a bootable BACKUP on a local disk
  was replaced by @SYS$SYSTEM:AXPVMS$PCSI_INSTALL_MIN.COM.   (And the
  newer versions of the "stub" STABACKIT procedure now optionally invoke
  this command procedure for you.)

:  Is that in any way like the old standalone backup boot ?

  The new environment occupies more space, but this is not a factor with
  the CD-ROM -- it _can_ be a factor for those excessively tight on disk
  space that don't have or want CD-ROM.  (All OpenVMS Alpha systems are
  required to have access to a CD-ROM for support and distributions, and
  the drives themselves are dropping in price.)

  The environment of the bootable CD-ROM is OpenVMS -- it's far superior
  to the traditional "standalone BACKUP" environment, as it allows one to
  directly access and repair problems that might crop up on the primary
  system disk, etc., without requiring a complete restoration.

  For further details, please take a look at the new features manual, and
