etxjesm@eds.ericsson.se wrote:

:   Does this mean that this system actualy is bootable from
:   another disk and not only the CD ? Is that in any way like
:   the old standalone backup boot ?

Yes, I've set mine up and it does boot from another disk.
It's similar to standalone abckup, except:

It's a subset of VMS.  Commands other than BACKUP may work (most do, but only
BACKUP is promised to work).

You have to hit return after the boot finishes, this autologin's to the
SYSTEM account (from the console ONLY).  The SYSUAF it's using is otherwize
basically empty.  You could run authorize and change this behaviour.

You should use sys$system:shutdown to reboot back to full VMS when you're done,
not just halt, this will dismount the disks cleanly (disks and tapes are 
mounted by BACKUP, or you can mount them yourself; standalone backup didn't
employ the mount concept).

It's full BACKUP, so you don't have to do image backups, which standalone 
backup always did whether you said /image or not.

It take much more disk space than standalone backup.

