>they remain the much smarter choice.

Network Computers will have a market in the home, possibly built into
other devices, TVs, Cable TV receivers etc.  

The good thing about the current NC craze from anyones point of view
is that the PC manufacturers have had to do a little rethinking.  
Companies have started selling `low spec' PCs, perfectly good enough
if all you want is word processing and a bit of net access, before
the NC threat these machines fell off the bottom of the price lists
of the major manufacturers - you just couldn't buy them.

