DECforms is Digital's commercial implementation (as opposed to prototypes
and lab work floating around at DEC and elsewhere) of the ISO 11730 1994E
Form Interface Management System standard.  The architecture is certainly
capable of doing client-server; workload partitioning and an application
messaging protocol is designed in.

There are certainly lots of options when connecting desktops to VMS
servers.  It really depends on the particulars of your environment and
"look and feel" requirements.  Of course, as a contributor to ISO 11730,
I'm biased.  ;-)  Contact me off-line and I'll get on my soapbox.





