In article <4shc6t$3t0@Mercury.mcs.com>, fluke@MCS.COM (Greg Linder) writes:
>	I recently picked up a used VAXStation 3100 m38 at a Hamfest. The
>machine has installed in it 16 megs ram total and 400 megs of disk space
>via 2 rz23's. The machine works fine, but it gives me a funky error when I
>power the machine up. After it runs through the diagnostics, it informs me
>of the following:
>
>	? 6 80A1  0000.4001

You don't have anything hooked up to SCSI bus B.  This only gets a single '?',
since it's not a fatal error.  Try a >>> SHOW DEVICE and see what's connected
where.  SCSI bus B is both internal, and is connected to the external port.

>       ?? 1 00C0  0000.7004

Look on the back of the machine to find the AUI and Thinwire connectors. 
Between them is a slide switch.  The switch selects either the AUI or Thinwire
network port. The error code says that you don't have anything connected to the
selected port.  The self-test tries to send a packet on the network and see it
come back (external loopback).  The error says that the packet didn't come
back.


