Jacky Kwok wrote:
> 
> My DEC ALPHA XL266 run Windows NT always has an error. NT crash and
> go into blue screen. An error "parity error: Dcache fill ....".
> 
> Is this a hardware error or software error?
> What is Dcache fill?
> 
> Jacky Kwok,
> Compose System Ltd.
> http://www.compose-sys.com

Hi Jacky,

When the Dcache (inside the Alpha CPU) has a miss, a request is sent 
outside the chip for the data. Assuming the Bcache (a bigger cache 
located near the CPU) also missed, the data is going to come from main 
memory (the SIMMs). You probably have a bad SIMM. Was there any more 
information displayed such as control and status register contents? There 
are many hardware registers that contain detailed information that can 
help identify the failing part.
Some operating systems do a better job than others at capturing the 
information.

The service guide for the Alpha XL 266 is available from:
    http://www.alphastation.digital.com 
    Click on Alpha XL, then click on Alpha XL Service Guides.

