] glew@ichips.intel.com (Andy Glew) writes:
] >What are the problems?
[...]
] >If they are interesting to any significant proportion of the
] >marketplace,
]
] I see you have a catch-all disclaimer.  Handy, that.

It's not a disclaimer, but a definition of scope.  Think
of it as the difference between someone trying to build
a motor for the fastest current gasoline-powered vehicle, 
versus someone building a motor for the fastest current
LOX+LH  (liquid oxygen and liquid hydrogen) powered vehicle.
Two different design spaces, two different markets, and the 
results (e.g. a Lamborgini automobile and a Saturn 5 rocket)
will not be similar, though both will be admirable.

You can talk about "P6 vs Alpha" in terms of differences.
But you really can't talk in terms of an absolute "better".
Each is better at some things than the other, which is not
suprising, since each is targetting different markets.
