:that you needed at least VMS 6.0 to use >=1GB drives on VAX systems.

  OpenVMS prior to V6.0 is limited to drives of 8.5GB or less, versions
  V6.0 and later are limited to 1TB, and all VAXstation 3100 system disks
  are (forever -- all OpenVMS versions) limited to 1.073GB or less.

  As others have mentioned, check the Digital patch area for any relevent
  patches -- there are a number of patches posted there.

  Also realize that V5.5-x is *old* -- the current release of OpenVMS is
  V7.0, and V7.1 is in field test.

