: I have a BA200 that has 2 DHV11s and 1 DZQ11. Problem is TTA doesnot show 
: up. both txa and txb does. With no docs I am wondering is this config 
: possible and really with txa and txb do I really need the DZQ??? 

If you've changed the complement of boards at all, you probably have
to reconfigure the CSR addresses on the serial boards.  Use the
shoadrs utility to obtain the correct CSR addresses for all boards,
then be sure the DIP switches or jumpers are set accordingly.  It
is helpful to have the docs to do this, because solving the chinese
puzzle of what DIP switches map to what bits of the CSR is tedious
to solve.

