Hi

We have just been told by a DEC reseller that we cannot deploy 2 PCI disk 
controllers to perform hardware disk mirrorring.  1st controller is for 
the primary set of disks while the 2nd controller is for the mirror 
disks.  This is most puzzling since previously we've disk mirrors on 
other systems such as HP & Sun on separate controllers without problem.  
Can somebody familiar with DEC Alpha products verify this ?

The controller in question is the 3-port PCI Backplane RAID Controller 
model KZPSC-BA.  The DEC Systems & Options Catalog also mentions that the 
internal storage assemblies can be configured for split bus mode to 
support wide mode on the first bus and narrow mode on the second bus.  
Therefore, can the following SCSI connections on the Alpha Server 
2100/275 cabinet be achieved such that the first 6 Wide SCSI disks on 
the 1st Bay are mirrored onto 6 Narrow SCSI disks on the 2nd Bay ?

                1st Bay		2nd Bay
		   W----|	   N----|
		   W----|	   N----|
		   W----|	   N----|
		   W----|---|	   N----|---|
		   W----|---|	   N----|---|
		   W----|---|	   N----|---|
		   W----|---|---|  W----|---|---|
		   W----|---|---|  W----|---|---|
			|   |	|	|   |	|
		   I=---|   |	|  I=---|   |	|
		   I=-------|	|  I=-------|	|
		   I=-----------|  I=-----------|
		PCI Controller 1   PCI Controller 2

W=Wide SCSI2 disk
N=Narrow SCSI2 disk
I=Single Port of PCI Disk Controller

