     door fly".  Intel has been consistently adept at bringing
     in process innovations and hitting the "sweet spot" in the
     trade-off between performance and cost for the PC market
     It also can leverage its incredible margins back into process
     and fab development.

>their ability to do aggressive circuit design to push clock rate;
>they have a reputation for creative circuit design.  I am not as
>familiar with MIPS, unfortunately.   

     DEC also shows remarkable ability to turn out products on
     time with previously published roadmaps and above the expected
     performance.  The FX!32 system also represents an immpressive
