    So what. Four and eight bit microcontrollers sell in the billions of
    units per year.  For end-user programmable systems (i.e. general
    purpose, non-embedded computers) the total revenue generated by the
    systems is more important than counting CPU sockets.  Last year RISC
    processor based systems brought in about $26 billion and its growth
    rate for at least the last two years has been far higher (>60%) than
    the growth rate for $40 (?) billion PC industry (~20%).  Also, for
    the RISC system manufacturers making money was the rule rather the
