   board and server development when its "screwdriver" competitors can
   buy four way SMP P6 boards from Intel and beat them to market.  The
   PC makers beat each others brains out trying to differentiate identical
   products while Intel builds Pentiums for $40 or less and sells them for
   $200-$500.  Soon some of these guys are going to realize that they are
   in a losing game and will look for a different business model.

