   loses, sometimes really big, on all four counts) and x86/DOS-Windows
   compatibility is irrelevent.  The first day sales of the 64 bit MIPS
   based Nintendo 64 video game in Japan was 300,000 machines and they
   expect to better that in the U.S.  These sales represent consumer
   dollars (or Yen) that might have otherwise gone to low end PC sales.
   The network computer represents a similar threat to Intel and MS as
   the potential global volumes could eclipse the total PC market (the
   businesses and consumers in second and third world countries can't
