These work perfectly well on Alpha. We have ported a large system which uses
FMS from VAX to Alpha with no problems (on the FMS side). There is a change to
the link step if you use compiled-in forms;

On VAX you would do something like this:

 $ LINK myprog, mylib/INCLUDE=(FDV$VECTOR,FDV$MEMRES)

On alpha you would do this:

 $ LINK myprog, mylib/INCLUDE=(FDV$LINKAGE,FDV$MEMRES)

but I can't recall any other problems. We have tended to migrate off FMS to
either Motif, or a home-grown utility which is a "Motif alike" for VT
terminals, based on SMG$ routines. The latter is called Bodgets :-) Sad eh ?

