pgrasso@usa1.com wrote:
> 
> Just in case any of you run into this...
> 
> When setting up an Alpha 2000 for RAID-5 and NT, Make Sure You
> Do the Following:
> 
> 1)  Burn DEC's Installation Instructions...
> 2)  DEC Recommends that you setup a RAID configured ALPHA with
> the partion as N-6Megs, Then setting up a 6MEG System Partion.
> Do the opposite, setup the system partion first...
> 3)  DEC Recommends that you select the "Standard VGA" during NT
> setup.  Instead, MAKE SURE YOU INSTALL THE CORRECT
> VIDEO DRIVER... Or else you will get an ambigous error message
> and the system will continously reboot to an infinate loop...
> 
> Otherwise, all went very well...
> 
> -Peter
> 
Actually, depending on which system you do this on, the VGA setting may
be the best.  In your case, with a 2000, you should be able to pick
either the VGA or the specific driver.  On a AlphaServer 1000, you MUST
have the "special" driver floppy shipped with the machine (or available
on the Web), because the built-in video (Cirrus) and NT 3.5/3.51 don't
get along in VGA mode.

In terms of configuring RAID (of whatever type), just be sure to have a
small (~6 MB) FAT partition on your system drive.  You can make the
other partitions on that drive whatever size you want, as long as you
have enough room on one to put NT.

Mark
