James L. Heid wrote:
> 
> This happened to me on OpenVMS VAX V6.1 running DEC C V5.0-003
> 
> There is a real application behind all this, but I will post the results of a
> test in the hope that someone can explain what is happening.
> 
> while ((c = fgetc(fp) != EOF)
>           putc(c, outfile);
> 

The precedence of "!=" is higher than that of "=" which means that
the evaluation order will be:

  while ( c = (fgetc(fp) != EOF) )

While the test for EOF will work okay, the assignment will be whatever
the inequality results are.  Try adding parens:

  while ( (c = fgetc(fp)) != EOF )



