> 
> Well, that's what it used to be. In light of the latest developments in
> the Reorg That Wouldn't Die, "All Busted Up" is an apropos translation of
> ABU.
> 
Well, actually the ABU isn't really going away.

The Accounts Business Unit was the group that sold to major large
accounts.  Products sold by the ABU were sourced from the Systems
Business Unit (SBU) and other BU's.

The recent reorganization was to consolidate the selling organizations
into one BU, but with several selling groups.  The Corporate Accounts
Group still will be covering the major accounts.  The General Accounts
Group will sell to the other accounts, with the major source of product
for these accounts to come from the reseller channel.  

The good news of this is that more customers will again have a Digital
selling rep.  This sales person may have lots of accounts, so don't
expect that person to be there every day.  However, you won't have to
hunt for someone from a distributor or reseller to get you a quote.

This will also cut down on some of the overhead of 2 business units,
which means cost savings, the true purpose of the re-organization.

Mark 
Southeast Technical Support Consultant

All opinions my own - not an official spokesperson for Digital....



