> What I need is the meaning of each field and the various bit maps.
> Can somebody please look in the relevant manual.

  The SID is split into a CPU model and model-dependent bits. The model-
dependent bits vary greatly depending on the CPU model. For example, on
older VAXen they were a real serial number (well, part of one anyway)
while on newer systems they sometimes indicated hardware revision infor-
mation.

  Your best source of information is the CPU manuals for the various
CPU models you're interested in.

