Let's hope not. It is my understanding that the merged ABU/SBU will
service somewhere between 1200 and 1500 customers. Customer calls DECrep
and places order. Order fulfillment in many cases will be via an Avnet,
WYLE, Pioneer, et al.

This is good for the customer because he or she can call a DECrep instead
of being shunted off to a channel partner's 800 number.

This is good for DEC because the firm has more control over the sales
cycle. After all, if a customer calls DEC for a Rawhide system and is
given the phone number of a partner, said partner may convince the
customer to buy competitive iron. Especially if the competitive iron comes
with a more generous discount.

A significant proportion of the 7K headcount reduction announced on July 2
will come from the SBU. Accordingly, methinks that the SBU's ability to
compete with channels partners will be greatly reduced.

