X-Deja-AN: 167854970
organization: University Communications, Inc.
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


There seems to be a bug in csh that exists in 4.0 and does not exist in 3.2D.

This can be demonstrated with the following:

echo 'abc {abc} abc' *

as compared to:

echo 'abc {abc} abc' woof

The existence of the opening brace, along with any argument containing
wildcards (? or *) will eliminate the entire first argument to echo
(the closing brace doesn't matter). It also happens with square bracket.
It doesn't matter how the braces are escaped (quotes or backslash),
nor does it matter if the built-in echo or /bin/echo is used.



