In article <4rs014$cj0@news.telia.se>,  <sysplj@kvaxt1.data.telia.se> wrote:
>I have a System Industries exabyte tape station that does not seem to 
>assign it's units to VMS. When selecting either port A or B from the VAX
>it's light is lit on the tape control panel, so I suppose there's a 
>connection, but no units appear as devices.
>Could it be that it need some kind of software to load or some other 
>tape-controller, other than the SDI-port on the uVAX 3600.

I'm unfamiliar with this particular SI tape drive, but I do know
that the SDI port on your uVax 3600 (presumably on a KDA50) sits
at a MSCP (disk) CSR, not a TMSCP (tape) CSR.  As a result, the MU
tape driver will never recognize it.  I'd hazard a guess
that you need special SI-supplied MU *and* DU drivers for this
rather bizarre piece of hardware.

Tim. (shoppa@triumf.ca)



