Abraham Kololli (ekololli@xmission.com) wrote:

: We are migrating from VAX5.5-2 to AXP 6.1 on a VAX7000-620.
: Does anyone know if there is any problems or concerns when we migrate
: from VAX to AXP and have different flavors of terminal servers like
: 200, 250, 300, and 700 around?

: How does the AXP affect the download images that these old terminal
: servers use?

The LAT DECservers download via the MOP_MOM Down Line Load (DLI)
protocol, which you will have to set up on the Alpha.  They connect
via the DEC LAT Protocol, which you will also have to run on all
hosts.  Digital Unix normally includes LAT.  DLI MOP_MOM may be
an option that you will have to set up, and you will have to
set up the various images for each model DECserver that requires
a Down Line Load Boot.

