Joesph Fenn <jfenn@spartacus.hula.net> writes:
|>I dont know how much difference in the two vt100 vs vt102 emulations.

The only difference between VT100 and VT102 is that the VT102 included the
printer port and the "Advanced Video Option" (which allowed you to display
132 columns by 24 lines) - these were optional on the VT100.  Most "VT100"
emulators really emulate a VT102.

I don't think your Lynx problems are related to this, but I have no idea
as to what the real problem might be.
