Is this one known?  Is there a fix?

Briefly, code taking the address of a function parameter declared float 
in the old style is not compiled correctly.

Here is a sample program

#include <stdio.h>

static void G(px)
     float *px;
{
  (void) printf("%f\n", *px);
}

static void F(x)
     float x;
{
  (void) printf("%f\n", x);
  G(&x);
}

int main ()
{
  F(0.2);
  return(0);
}

Here is its output:

axpfeb{66} cc -std0 bug.c -o bug
axpfeb{67} bug
0.200000
-0.000000
axpfeb{68} 

