We are using PrintServer Software for OSF/1 AXP LPSBASE500 to print to our
DEC PrintServer 17 printer.  The software created the following printcap file:

lps17|lps17 (PrintServer lps17):\
        :lp=/dev/null-lps17:\
        :sd=/var/spool/lps17:\
        :of=/usr/opt/LPS/bin/OSF1_V1.3/lpsof:\
        :if=/usr/opt/LPS/bin/OSF1_V1.3/lpsif:\
        :lf=/var/adm/lps17.log:\
        :pl#66:pw#80:mx#0:sb:

We need to add a DVI print filter (df) to the printcap file in order to
convert DVI files to PostScript for the printer.  We have done this in the
past when the printer was connected via an Ultrix host.

We added:

        :df=/usr/local/bin/lps20_TeXdvi:\

lps20_TeXdvi simply sends stdin to dvips which sends PostScript through
stdout.

Unfortunately, lpsof (the output filter) doesn't like this:

lpsof   Jun 28 14:35:21:  Session started for Job 0 (root@wpi.WPI.EDU), lps17 job number is 327
