  The DECmailer program is certainly worthwhile (I have had a DECmailer
account for years - in the DM4xx range). However, for the hobbyist it has
a number of drawbacks:

  1) the module repair cost is likely to be several orders of magnitude more
     than they paid for the complete system
  2) the hobbyist may not have a spare module set to use to discover which
     one of a related set of modules is bad
  3) the DECmailer catalog doesn't list the majority of the M-series modules
     because many modules aren't eligible for DECmailer coverage
  4) DECmailer won't accept burned boards in most cases, and they may reject
     boards with non-DEC FCO's applied (like customer-made or ESS, etc.)

  In general, I look at the DECmailer price and compare it to the price of
a module on the used/surplus market. Sometimes DECmailer is cheaper, some-
times not.

