newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


Dear folks on the Internet,

we'd like to report a problem of network integration using DEC-only
products which made us quite insecure about DEC's product management:

Our LAN has a pretty simple layout: There are seven peripheral
DEChub90's, each with a DECbridge90FL, connected to a central
DEChub90, where among other components a DECagent 90 is responsible
for SNMP management.

This infrastructure is roughly two years old, so the major part of the
components consists of DECrepeater90T (eight port).

Expecting a smooth integration we ordered some DECrepeater90T16's to
expand our LAN, and had to learn that those components are not
manageable with the DECbridge90FL due to changes in the data format of
the management information.  Thus, the DECrepeater90T16's could only
be deployed in the central hub, where the DECagent90 is willing to
adopt them, but where we don't need so many of them.

Now it seems to us that a product aged two years should be capable to
cooperate with a new product of our days, but this doesn't seem to be
true with the HUB-family products...

Looking for a workaround, we learned that DECrepeater90T16's can be
managed with the new DECrepeater90TS. As tests showed, this would mean
a complete other strategy in SNMP data collection (several agents
throughout the LAN instead of one central agent). Indeed, the *new*
component DECrepeater90T16 could be managed using the *new*
DECrepeater90TS, but, having transferred the hub mastership from the
DECbridge90FL to the DECrepeater90TS, our *old* DECbridge90FL couldn't
be managed, though.

The next idea on the way to get our LAN extended, was to simply order
the tried-and-tested DECrepeater90T's.

Now we had to learn that these parts can't be obtained any more, the
DECrepeater90TS is the only successor. This DECrepeater90TS, like the
DECrepeater90T16, can't be managed with the DECbridge90, so we find
ourselves in a blind alleyway, where all these fine DECbriges on our
LAN seem to finally turn out to be a bad investment!

We'd like to ask if there is anybody out there having experienced
similar problems. Perhaps it doesn't look so bad if someone would
outline the product strategy that lead to this confusion. Digital
Germany couldn't!

Regards,

