In article <4r136v$ej0@medulla.ama.ttuhsc.edu>, sean@cortex (Sean Dougherty) writes:
>Has anybody tried to put a Micropolis 3243 into a DEC 3000 running OSF 3.2C?
>
>I'm trying that very thing and need a disktab entry.

If the drive is well behaved and puts its geometry information in the
conventional place, the disklabel command will be able to get it and
won't need a disktab entry.  It will also get the default partition
table from the driver:

# disklabel -wr /dev/rrz#c micropolis

I've heard of some drives that aren't well behaved, so it if doesn't
work, keep trying to find a disktab entry.
